cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Exhaustive search outperforms a genetic algorithm for
  formulary-constrained antiretroviral regimen selection
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaudat Faisal
    family-names: Al-Husein
    email: jaudatalhusein@gmail.com
    affiliation: Antioch Private University, Rural Damascus, Syria
  - given-names: Omar Ali
    family-names: Al-Khayat
    affiliation: Antioch Private University, Rural Damascus, Syria
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jaudat150/art-regimen-selection-with-GA'
doi: '10.5281/zenodo.22809521'
abstract: >-
  WHO-compliant first-line antiretroviral regimen selection formulated
  as constrained combinatorial optimisation, comparing a genetic
  algorithm against exhaustive search over a provably identical
  feasible set. The genetic algorithm reaches the exact optimum for
  every patient while performing roughly 1,400 times more computation;
  for 15 of 17 patients the optimum is already present in its randomly
  initialised population.
keywords:
  - combinatorial optimisation
  - exact algorithms
  - genetic algorithms
  - antiretroviral therapy
  - clinical decision support
  - benchmarking
  - negative results
